{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-159778",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "Recall that if $X=[{X}_{1},{X}_{2}]^{T}$ is a bivariate normal random vector with mean vector $\\mu $ and covariance matrix $Σ,$ given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mu =[\\begin{aligned}{\\mu }_{1} \\\\ {\\mu }_{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,Σ=[\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }_{1}^{2} & {\\sigma }_{12} \\\\ {\\sigma }_{21} & {\\sigma }_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nthen the random variable $Y,$ defined as\n\n$$\nY=a{X}_{1}+b{X}_{2}\n$$\n\nis a normally distributed random variable for all values of $a$ and $b,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}E[Y] & =a{\\mu }_{1}+b{\\mu }_{2}, \\\\ Var[Y] & ={a}^{2}{\\sigma }_{1}^{2}+{b}^{2}{\\sigma }_{2}^{2}+2ab{\\sigma }_{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have ${\\mu }_{1}=5$ and ${\\mu }_{2}=1.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[Y] & =\\text{E}[{X}_{1}+3{X}_{2}] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{X}_{1}]+3\\text{E}[{X}_{2}] \\\\  & ={\\mu }_{1}+3\\cdot {\\mu }_{2} \\\\  & =5+3\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, we have ${\\sigma }_{1}^{2}=1,{\\sigma }_{2}^{2}=5,$ and ${\\sigma }_{12}={\\sigma }_{21}=-2.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Var[Y] & =Var[{X}_{1}+3{X}_{2}] \\\\  & ={1}^{2}\\cdot 1+{3}^{2}\\cdot 5+2\\cdot 1\\cdot 3\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =1+45-12 \\\\  & =34.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\nY∼N(8,34).\n$$\n\nNow, we need to compute $P(1\\le Y\\le 5).$ First, transform $Y$ into a standard normal random variable $Z$ by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(1\\le Y\\le 5) & =P(\\frac{1-8}{\\sqrt{34}}\\le Z\\le \\frac{5-8}{\\sqrt{34}}) \\\\  & =P(-1.20\\le Z\\le -0.51)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we express the required probability in terms of $Φ(z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-1.20\\le Z\\le -0.51) & =P(Z\\le -0.51)-P(Z<-1.20) \\\\  & =P(Z\\le -0.51)-P(Z\\le -1.20) \\\\  & =Φ(-0.51)-Φ(-1.20)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the table, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Φ(-1.20) & =0.1151 \\\\ Φ(-0.51) & =0.3050\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-1.20\\le Z\\le -0.51) & =Φ(-0.51)-Φ(-1.20) \\\\  & =0.3050-0.1151 \\\\  & =0.1899.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we conclude that\n\n$$\nP(1\\le Y\\le 5)=0.1899.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
